1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,768
Millions of people own stocks.

2
00:00:01,818 --> 00:00:03,822
On Robinhood Chain, stocks are tokens,

3
00:00:03,872 --> 00:00:05,815
but a token earns nothing while it sits.

4
00:00:05,865 --> 00:00:08,060
Wall Street holders sell
covered calls for income,

5
00:00:08,111 --> 00:00:10,055
but someone must pick each week's strike,

6
00:00:10,105 --> 00:00:11,117
and you must trust them.

7
00:00:11,167 --> 00:00:12,135
On-chain it's harder:

8
00:00:12,186 --> 00:00:13,963
multipliers easy to apply twice,

9
00:00:14,013 --> 00:00:15,153
weekend price freezes,

10
00:00:15,203 --> 00:00:16,547
pauses, mid-week splits.

11
00:00:16,597 --> 00:00:17,902
So tokens sit idle,

12
00:00:17,952 --> 00:00:19,765
or go to managers nobody can check.

13
00:00:19,815 --> 00:00:22,491
Now imagine an agent picking
the strike each week,

14
00:00:22,541 --> 00:00:24,137
held to the rules by a contract.

15
00:00:24,187 --> 00:00:24,937
This is Strike:

16
00:00:24,987 --> 00:00:26,722
options vaults for stock tokens.

17
00:00:26,772 --> 00:00:28,594
Weekly premium in USDG.

18
00:00:28,644 --> 00:00:31,307
An AI agent picks the
strike, inside a mandate.

19
00:00:31,357 --> 00:00:33,745
Break it, and its bond goes to depositors.

20
00:00:33,795 --> 00:00:35,483
Rust on Stylus does the math.

21
00:00:35,533 --> 00:00:38,368
Live on Robinhood Chain
and Arbitrum Sepolia.

22
00:00:38,418 --> 00:00:39,431
Inside one week:

23
00:00:39,481 --> 00:00:41,661
Depositors fill a vault
with a fixed mandate.

24
00:00:41,711 --> 00:00:44,308
An agent reads it via MCP and dry-runs.

25
00:00:44,358 --> 00:00:46,980
It proposes delta, expiry, size and price.

26
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:49,760
The Epoch Manager checks it
at guarded oracle prices.

27
00:00:49,810 --> 00:00:52,076
Rust on Stylus solves and
stress-tests the strike.

28
00:00:52,126 --> 00:00:54,898
If it passes, buyers pay premium in USDG.

29
00:00:54,948 --> 00:00:57,170
If not, the bond is slashed to depositors.

30
00:00:57,220 --> 00:00:58,781
Decisions are hashed on-chain;

31
00:00:58,831 --> 00:01:01,617
the agent has an ERC-8004 identity.

32
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:02,812
Friday's close settles;

33
00:01:02,862 --> 00:01:05,080
depositors get the premium, less a fee.

34
00:01:05,130 --> 00:01:08,332
Same contracts on Robinhood
Chain and Arbitrum Sepolia.

35
00:01:08,382 --> 00:01:10,070
Say Maya opens the Tesla vault.

36
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:14,257
Its first week sold the $369.86 call:

37
00:01:14,307 --> 00:01:16,325
four options, 10.01 USDG.

38
00:01:16,375 --> 00:01:18,475
At or below the strike, Maya keeps it;

39
00:01:18,525 --> 00:01:21,743
the buyer profits above $372.36.

40
00:01:21,793 --> 00:01:23,222
The limits are in the contract:

41
00:01:23,272 --> 00:01:25,937
Delta 0.10 to 0.35,

42
00:01:25,987 --> 00:01:28,161
at least 95% of fair value,

43
00:01:28,211 --> 00:01:30,619
at least 0.05% yield,

44
00:01:30,669 --> 00:01:32,049
at most 80% sold,

45
00:01:32,099 --> 00:01:32,979
1 to 8 days,

46
00:01:33,029 --> 00:01:33,996
fixed for good.

47
00:01:34,046 --> 00:01:35,914
The playground tests proposals live,

48
00:01:35,964 --> 00:01:36,584
no wallet.

49
00:01:36,634 --> 00:01:39,297
An honest 0.20-delta call: accepted.

50
00:01:39,347 --> 00:01:41,027
A reckless at-the-money strike:

51
00:01:41,077 --> 00:01:42,694
rejected, delta out of band.

52
00:01:42,744 --> 00:01:46,746
A real one costs the agent
10 USDG, paid to depositors.

53
00:01:46,796 --> 00:01:48,522
Buyers pay at the moment they buy:

54
00:01:48,572 --> 00:01:51,258
oracle spot moved 0.5% against them,

55
00:01:51,308 --> 00:01:53,509
Black-Scholes, times the agent's factor.

56
00:01:53,559 --> 00:01:55,018
Never below intrinsic value,

57
00:01:55,068 --> 00:01:57,089
so stale prices can't be picked off.

58
00:01:57,139 --> 00:01:58,775
Buying waits for the NYSE open,

59
00:01:58,825 --> 00:02:00,532
shown in your own time zone.

60
00:02:00,582 --> 00:02:04,415
Live on September 29, the seller
agent asked for 0.20 delta;

61
00:02:04,465 --> 00:02:08,312
the contract solved $369.86, accepted.

62
00:02:08,362 --> 00:02:10,600
A reckless agent forced
an at-the-money put:

63
00:02:10,650 --> 00:02:12,620
rejected, 10 USDG slashed,

64
00:02:12,670 --> 00:02:14,218
bond 60 to 50.

65
00:02:14,268 --> 00:02:17,503
The explorer says Success:
a rejection isn't a revert,

66
00:02:17,553 --> 00:02:19,586
and 10 USDG left the bond.

67
00:02:19,636 --> 00:02:22,200
The call expired Friday at 20:00 UTC;

68
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:23,299
it has not settled yet.

69
00:02:23,349 --> 00:02:26,249
It settles at the first mainnet
Chainlink print after expiry;

70
00:02:26,299 --> 00:02:28,287
the contract rejects any other price.

71
00:02:28,337 --> 00:02:31,542
The last print, at 19:55,
came before expiry.

72
00:02:31,592 --> 00:02:33,932
The epoch trace shows
each step's transaction,

73
00:02:33,982 --> 00:02:35,127
and what is pending.

74
00:02:35,177 --> 00:02:37,449
Anyone can run an agent,
with no permission.

75
00:02:37,499 --> 00:02:39,470
Here a test wallet registers an agent

76
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:42,229
and bonds 60 USDG, above the 50 minimum.

77
00:02:42,279 --> 00:02:43,541
The wallet signs each step:

78
00:02:43,591 --> 00:02:44,909
register, then bond.

79
00:02:44,959 --> 00:02:48,164
Each one waits for its block
on Robinhood Chain testnet.

80
00:02:49,264 --> 00:02:50,404
Now it can propose.

81
00:02:50,454 --> 00:02:53,744
Every rejected proposal costs it 10 USDG.

82
00:02:58,277 --> 00:03:00,377
On Arbitrum Sepolia, Claude planned it:

83
00:03:00,427 --> 00:03:03,059
via Strike's MCP server, it read the vault

84
00:03:03,109 --> 00:03:04,807
and dry-ran five candidates.

85
00:03:04,857 --> 00:03:08,439
It chose 0.20 delta at 105% of fair value,

86
00:03:08,489 --> 00:03:09,447
and wrote why:

87
00:03:09,497 --> 00:03:11,387
mid-band, safe from small moves.

88
00:03:11,437 --> 00:03:15,005
The contract solved $364.29: accepted.

89
00:03:15,055 --> 00:03:15,773
On Arbiscan:

90
00:03:15,823 --> 00:03:17,752
a successful call from the agent's signer.

91
00:03:17,802 --> 00:03:20,349
The same run slashed a
reckless put 10 USDG,

92
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,087
and a buyer took all 4 calls.

93
00:03:22,137 --> 00:03:22,917
In 3D:

94
00:03:22,967 --> 00:03:25,898
Across, Tesla's price. Back, days left.

95
00:03:25,949 --> 00:03:27,339
Up, a share's value.

96
00:03:27,389 --> 00:03:31,200
At expiry it bends flat
at the $364.29 strike:

97
00:03:31,251 --> 00:03:32,644
upside goes to the buyer.

98
00:03:32,694 --> 00:03:36,537
Below, the depositor keeps
stock plus $2.23 per option.

99
00:03:36,587 --> 00:03:38,717
The math is Rust, on Arbitrum Stylus.

100
00:03:38,767 --> 00:03:41,181
Solving a strike takes
48 Black-Scholes runs:

101
00:03:41,231 --> 00:03:43,517
6.5 times less gas than Solidity,

102
00:03:43,567 --> 00:03:45,810
3.3 times less per proposal.

103
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:47,468
Every run leaves a decision record.

104
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:49,532
Its hash is anchored in the DecisionLog;

105
00:03:49,582 --> 00:03:51,748
rehash the file, and it matches the chain.

106
00:03:51,798 --> 00:03:54,313
CI re-checks every cited transaction:

107
00:03:54,363 --> 00:03:56,925
160 of 160 verified.

108
00:03:56,975 --> 00:03:58,674
Each proposal gets a decision page.

109
00:03:58,724 --> 00:04:00,772
Agent two's put on October 2:

110
00:04:00,822 --> 00:04:02,133
each mandate rule it passed,

111
00:04:02,183 --> 00:04:03,360
with the headroom left.

112
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:04,501
Why not the other strikes:

113
00:04:04,551 --> 00:04:07,132
the same proposal at each
delta, judged by the rules.

114
00:04:07,182 --> 00:04:08,700
And what would make this week lose:

115
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:10,830
TSLA below $340.20,

116
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,821
17% odds under the model.

117
00:04:12,871 --> 00:04:14,223
Agent one's forced put:

118
00:04:14,273 --> 00:04:16,018
rejected, delta out of band.

119
00:04:16,068 --> 00:04:17,116
The check stops there;

120
00:04:17,166 --> 00:04:18,745
later rules are never reached.

121
00:04:18,795 --> 00:04:20,793
Its ERC-8004 identity:

122
00:04:20,843 --> 00:04:25,588
114 on Robinhood Chain testnet,
253 on Arbitrum Sepolia.

123
00:04:25,638 --> 00:04:26,222
The monitor,

124
00:04:26,273 --> 00:04:27,326
live on mainnet:

125
00:04:27,376 --> 00:04:31,878
Nvidia's multiplier, 1.000775,
is already in the price,

126
00:04:31,928 --> 00:04:33,828
so Strike never applies it twice.

127
00:04:33,878 --> 00:04:36,404
Over 403 weeks since 2019,

128
00:04:36,454 --> 00:04:39,566
covered calls cut volatility 25 to 46%,

129
00:04:39,616 --> 00:04:41,145
but lagged holding everywhere:

130
00:04:41,195 --> 00:04:45,313
Tesla 23.1% a year, against 44.0% held.

131
00:04:45,363 --> 00:04:47,240
And it assumes full weekly sales.

132
00:04:47,290 --> 00:04:48,128
The proof page:

133
00:04:48,178 --> 00:04:50,341
1,393 tests and proofs,

134
00:04:50,391 --> 00:04:52,304
99.3% line coverage,

135
00:04:52,354 --> 00:04:53,482
nine Halmos proofs,

136
00:04:53,532 --> 00:04:55,248
all 11 review findings fixed.

137
00:04:55,298 --> 00:04:57,193
Running by itself reads both testnets:

138
00:04:57,243 --> 00:04:58,539
prices, each vault's week,

139
00:04:58,589 --> 00:04:59,636
the scheduled jobs.

140
00:04:59,686 --> 00:05:01,977
The mirror audit checks
every copied price:

141
00:05:02,027 --> 00:05:04,913
84 of 84 rounds match mainnet Chainlink.

142
00:05:04,963 --> 00:05:05,943
Who else is here?

143
00:05:05,993 --> 00:05:09,138
Stonkhouse and Archer Markets on
Robinhood Chain are order books:

144
00:05:09,188 --> 00:05:10,831
traders pick strike and price.

145
00:05:10,881 --> 00:05:13,751
Ribbon, Derive and Thetanuts
sell crypto options

146
00:05:13,801 --> 00:05:15,778
by auction, order book or RFQ.

147
00:05:15,828 --> 00:05:18,359
Tilt's AI manages vaults, with no options;

148
00:05:18,409 --> 00:05:21,463
its sources don't say
what limits it on-chain.

149
00:05:21,513 --> 00:05:23,585
In Strike, a bonded agent proposes,

150
00:05:23,636 --> 00:05:25,509
the contract enforces mandate and price,

151
00:05:25,559 --> 00:05:26,818
and rule-breakers pay.

152
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:29,015
Stock-token traps are handled on-chain.

153
00:05:29,065 --> 00:05:31,117
Holders get income and keep their keys.

154
00:05:31,167 --> 00:05:34,230
Weekend freezes: settle on
the first post-expiry price.

155
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:36,643
Multiplier: never applied, fork-tested.

156
00:05:36,693 --> 00:05:39,448
Agent trust: fixed
mandate, bond, slashing.

157
00:05:39,498 --> 00:05:42,370
Gas: Rust on Stylus, 6.5 times cheaper.

158
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:44,830
Not done: no audit, and testnet only.

159
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:47,369
Strike: options on Robinhood
Chain and Arbitrum,

160
00:05:47,419 --> 00:05:49,593
run by agents held to a mandate.
